-- ============================================================
-- 162 — THE FOROSNAÍ WATERS, SEEDED (nine rows of public.awen)
-- resonance-knowledge Supabase (qdzerwmsbksuhvczlwli)
--
-- SOURCE, and the only source of each definition:
-- resonance-forosnai/docs/THE-FOROSNAI-PLAN.md, the nine rows of the table
-- under "What still needs imagining" — one row per water, the first column
-- the slug. Each definition is that row's own what-it-does with its `in` and
-- its `out` columns and nothing outside them. Each story carries that row's
-- fifth column with flowing and imagined marked as the plan marks them, the
-- consumers the plan names in Part Two and Part Three, the mark and the step
-- from "The order and the marks", and the line of KP's naming.
--
-- THE REALM: founded 2026-09-15 at KP's word, quoted in the plan's opening,
-- "we are going to create a new repo for our own 'effects studio' calling it
-- 'resonance-forosnai'", and registered by 161-resonance-forosnai.sql.
--
-- NO ATOMS PAPER BEFORE THIS ONE: all nine atoms stand, read live 2026-09-15,
-- and each plural's "s" already stands in its atom's modifiers, so the plural
-- is the modifiers' work and the row rides the singular root (the-scrolls
-- precedent, 055). This paper stands on its own.
--
-- THE NINE ROWS — atom · tool_type · face:
--
--   the-effect      atom `effect`      STANDS (status, modifiers carry "s")
--     tool_type `transform` — a document's text becomes an effect and an
--       effect's parts become a document: the form changes, the truth does
--       not, and the round trip is byte-identical. Runner-up `translate`,
--       set down because translate carries meaning into another tongue and
--       these two shapes are one tongue.
--     face 🗒️ — a written sheet: the effect is a document. Runner-up 🎫,
--       set down because a ticket admits and this water declares.
--
--   the-graph       atom `graph`       STANDS (data)
--     tool_type `arrange` — nodes and typed edges placed in deliberate
--       relation, the evaluation order derived from them and the operations
--       given in order for one moment. Runner-up `transform`, set down
--       because the ordering is the work and the plan is its shape.
--     face 🔢 — the derived order and the counted cost. Runner-up 🔁, set
--       down because a cycle is the thing this water refuses by name.
--
--   the-dynamics    atom `dynamic`     STANDS (status, modifiers carry "s",
--                                      so the plural is the modifiers' work)
--     tool_type `transform` — a signal's value becomes a parameter's value
--       under a law held as data: one truth, another form. Runner-up
--       `combine`, set down because the law is read and not joined to the
--       signal.
--     face 🎢 — the rise and fall of a ride: a source followed through a
--       range under a curve. Runner-up 🔉, set down because a volume mark
--       names one source and this water takes many.
--
--   the-transition  atom `transition`  STANDS (lifecycle)
--     tool_type `combine` — two sources brought into one blend while each
--       stays recognisable inside it. Runner-up `arrange`, set down because
--       the span is given by the caller and the blend is the work.
--     face 🔦 — a beam moving across, the wipe that uncovers one source and
--       leaves the other. Runner-up ⏲️, set down because a timer counts a
--       span and this water blends across one.
--
--   the-screen      atom `screen`      STANDS (sensory)
--     tool_type `transform` — a plane of pixels in, a new plane out under a
--       described arithmetic: the form changes, the truth does not.
--       Runner-up `emit`, set down because the shader is one form this
--       water's description is sent out in and the arithmetic is the water.
--     face 🪟 — a pane: light in one side, changed light out, and the pane
--       is never the light. Runner-up 🧿, set down because a ringed bead
--       wards and this water computes.
--
--   the-particles   atom `particle`    STANDS (sensory, modifiers carry "s",
--                                      so the plural is the modifiers' work)
--     tool_type `arrange` — positions and looks placed in the plane at one
--       millisecond from laws and a seed. Runner-up `emit`, set down
--       because the house's emit is a sending outward in a rendered form
--       and this water resolves a field to keys.
--     face 🫧 — many small bodies born, carried and gone, each with its own
--       lifetime. Runner-up 🎆, set down because a firework is one burst
--       and an emitter runs on at a rate.
--
--   the-glyphs      atom `glyph`       STANDS (sensory, modifiers carry "s",
--                                      so the plural is the modifiers' work)
--     tool_type `arrange` — the parts of text laid by arithmetic, each part
--       given its transform at one moment. Runner-up `transform`, set down
--       because the laying is the work and each part's transform is what it
--       yields.
--     face 🪪 — a card's printed name: glyphs laid by arithmetic and kept
--       readable. Runner-up 🪡, set down because a needle sews a line and
--       this water lays parts.
--
--   the-resonance   atom `resonance`   STANDS (consciousness)
--     tool_type `capture` — it takes hold of a point passing across frames
--       so its track can be kept as keys. Runner-up `witness`, set down
--       because the confidence and the refusal are how it captures
--       honestly, not the whole of what it does.
--     face 👀 — eyes that follow one thing across frames. Runner-up 📹, set
--       down because a camera makes the frames and this water reads them.
--
--   the-wear        atom `wear`        STANDS (no category; modifiers carry
--                                      "s", "ing", "worn", "wore")
--     tool_type `witness` — it reads an effect's requirement and a host's
--       declaration and says worn, or names the lack; it attests and never
--       judges. Runner-up `combine`, set down because the two declarations
--       are read against each other and not joined.
--     face 🔋 — the charge a host must hold before a thing runs. Runner-up
--       🪜, set down because a ladder reaches and this water answers.
--
-- Unworn and left in this paper's pool: 🪩 🪡 📼 📹 🎠 🕹️ 🪈 🪣 🪜 🔉 🎷 🎺
-- 🪕 🪘 ⏲️ 🌿 🍃 🪵 🔁 🎫 🏟️ 🌀 🎆 🎇 🧿.
--
-- Every face is one grapheme, no skin tone, no ZWJ sequence, no flag, no
-- red-alarm mark, and none is worn by the 155 rows the spring carries today.
-- No two rows in this paper wear the same one. The live base may hold a face
-- this hand could not see, so the verify select below stands.
--
-- CATEGORY is a column of public.atoms and of no awen row — the parentheses
-- above record the category each standing atom already carries.
--
-- THE ONE-TIER LAW (tools_one_tier), walked: every name here is one word, so
-- every row carries atom_id and leaves molecule_id and organism_id null. One
-- tier exactly, nine times.
--
-- Etymology and sensory rows are not written here: the atoms stand and their
-- companions are the triggers' work.
--
-- STATUS IS `imagined` ON ALL NINE. Nothing here crosses to `flowing`: that is
-- KP's hand alone, and no update on public.awen stands in this paper. No
-- delete either; this paper only inserts.
--
-- THE LADDER: the features plan's ladder does not yet hold this realm, and
-- where it sits is KP's word, so no row here names a features-plan row. The
-- marks and the steps are the plan's own order table.
-- ============================================================

insert into public.awen
  (name, slug, tool_type, definition, home, status,
   atom_id, molecule_id, organism_id, story, created_by,
   folksonomy_type, icon_emoji)
values

-- 1 · the-effect
('The Effect', 'the-effect', 'transform',
 'The effect, as a document. An effect is a name and a kind — sound, picture, motion or face; the inputs it takes, each named by type: a plane of pixels, channels of samples, a reading, a state, a beat; its parameters as a tree of keys, each key carrying a law of type, range, default and unit; its steps as an ordered chain of named operations bound to those parameters; its tracks of keys over time; and its state map in the effects engine''s shape. In goes a document''s text, or an effect''s parts. Out comes the effect, or the document, and every break named. It is read and written whole: every key it does not know is kept, and the round trip is byte-identical.',
 'resonance-awen/tools/the-effect', 'imagined',
 (select id from public.atoms where atom_word = 'effect'), null, null,
 'WHAT STANDS BESIDE IT, as the plan marks it: the-board-charter''s grammar (flowing) and the-effects-engine''s state map (flowing); the shape of a parameter tree as the-rack describes it and of a chain as the-inserts does (both imagined). THE LAW IT CARRIES, the plan''s "The one law that shapes the split": an effect is a document — keys are stored and numbers are derived, the effects engine''s law A0 applied to every effect, and the pixels, the samples, the camera, the microphone, the GPU, the plugin binary and the window are the consumer''s dress. CONSUMERS: forosnaí first — Part Two''s wear room writes the effect as its document, signed with the-signet, sealed with the-sphragis, packaged with its assets by the-cofra — then every sibling studio the charter names as wearing what is made here: sistrum for sound, sceal for the moving picture, ardan for the stage, theophany for the face, cruthú for the still picture, khoros for what streams. GAPS IT ANSWERS, of the fifteen the research found (resonance-forosnai/docs/THE-EFFECTS-RESEARCH.md §5, as the plan reads them): 15, templates that break and invite copying — the same document opens in every version because unknown keys are kept; 12, hard to learn and tutorials out of step — the effect is readable as data and every law is named in the document. MARK: medium, step 1 of "The order and the marks" — the document born beside the-board-charter''s grammar, proofs on a round trip. It is the first water, everything hangs from it, and steps 1 to 6 need no app. One hand and one verifier, proofs in the water''s own folder, mirrored into its consumers by copy with a MIRROR.md. Described 2026-09-15 in resonance-forosnai/docs/THE-FOROSNAI-PLAN.md, the table under "What still needs imagining", drawn at KP''s ⚛ word: "then outline what flowing or imagined stand alone waters already exist to serve and what ones still need imagined." NAMED BY KP 2026-09-15, the line verbatim: "1- the-effect". Seeded imagined 2026-09-15 at KP''s ⚛ word.',
 'a platform hand, at KP''s ⚛ word',
 'Awen', '🗒️'),

-- 2 · the-graph
('The Graph', 'the-graph', 'arrange',
 'The graph and its plan. An effect''s steps stand as nodes and typed edges rather than one chain, so a mask can feed a blur and a composite at once, and a group is a node. The evaluation order is derived from the graph itself. A cycle, an edge whose types do not meet, and a node with an unbound input are each refused by name. For one moment it gives the plan: the operations in order with their resolved parameters, and the cost counted as operations on samples or pixels, so a preview can decide before it runs. In go a graph, a moment and the resolved parameters. Out come the ordered plan and its cost, or a refusal.',
 'resonance-awen/tools/the-graph', 'imagined',
 (select id from public.atoms where atom_word = 'graph'), null, null,
 'WHAT STANDS BESIDE IT, as the plan marks it: nothing flowing; the-stack''s resolution at a millisecond, the-inserts'' order and the-scene''s draw plan (all imagined); the-rack''s block plan is the same idea for audio alone, and the-graph''s typed edges, cycle refusal and cost are new. CONSUMERS: forosnaí first — Part Two''s bench holds the graph on a canvas, nodes as the waters and the standing effects, edges as typed data, parameters as controls read from each node''s tree, a group a node and opening one a walk into it; Part Two''s preview runs one moment as one plan from the-graph on the WebView, and the cost decides the preview''s size before the frame is drawn; Part Two''s timeline carries tracks of keys under the graph, groups as nodes, so the timeline never needs a pre-comp. Then the sibling studios the charter names as wearing what is made here: sistrum, sceal, ardan, theophany, cruthú and khoros. GAPS IT ANSWERS, of the fifteen the research found (resonance-forosnai/docs/THE-EFFECTS-RESEARCH.md §5, as the plan reads them): 13, no timeline groups — a group is a node in the graph and the graph is the timeline''s own shape; 4, 5, 7 and 8, one row in the plan (slow previews, crashes, hardware the maker does not have, caps discovered by rejection), of which this water answers the preview: a preview is a plan for one moment with its cost counted before it runs, so it degrades by law rather than freezing. MARK: medium, step 3 of "The order and the marks", after the-effect, the-dynamics and the-wear; steps 1 to 6 need no app. A RULING ON THE SAME PAGE: 0.21 was ruled 2026-09-15 — the plugin format is a build choice, drawn in 5.9''s own plan; the-rack is free to be drawn, and nothing in Part One waits on it. One hand and one verifier, proofs in the water''s own folder, mirrored into its consumers by copy with a MIRROR.md; a water whose consumer is itself imagined is mirrored the day that consumer is built. Described 2026-09-15 in resonance-forosnai/docs/THE-FOROSNAI-PLAN.md, the table under "What still needs imagining", drawn at KP''s ⚛ word: "then outline what flowing or imagined stand alone waters already exist to serve and what ones still need imagined." NAMED BY KP 2026-09-15, the line verbatim: "2- the-graph". Seeded imagined 2026-09-15 at KP''s ⚛ word.',
 'a platform hand, at KP''s ⚛ word',
 'Awen', '🔢'),

-- 3 · the-dynamics
('The Dynamics', 'the-dynamics', 'transform',
 'The modulation. A signal is mapped onto a parameter by a law held as data: the source — loudness, a band''s energy, a reading''s scalar, beat phase, breath phase, or a state token; the range; the curve between; the smoothing; the dead zone. The law resolves to the parameter''s value at a moment. In go a signal''s value, a modulation law and a moment. Out comes a parameter value. This is the studio''s logic, and it is data, never code: the source, the range, the curve between, the smoothing and the dead zone are each named in the law itself.',
 'resonance-awen/tools/the-dynamics', 'imagined',
 (select id from public.atoms where atom_word = 'dynamic'), null, null,
 'THE NAME IS PLURAL AND THE ATOM IS THE ROOT: `dynamic` already carries "s" in its modifiers, so the plural is the modifiers'' work (the-scrolls precedent, 055). WHAT STANDS BESIDE IT, as the plan marks it: the-kampyle''s curve and the-effects-engine''s state map (flowing); the-retarget''s thresholds and dead zones (imagined); the-inserts resolves a track over time, and the-dynamics is new because its source is a live signal rather than time. The signals it reads flow already, in Part One''s table: the-metronome''s beats, the-breath''s phase and the-temporal''s windows in time. CONSUMERS: forosnaí first — Part Two''s modulation board sets signals on the left, parameters on the right, and the laws between as the-dynamics rows; theophany, whose first effect in Part Three is a reading''s scalar through the-dynamics onto a part''s key, the alien''s glow when the brows rise. Then the sibling studios the charter names as wearing what is made here: sistrum, sceal, ardan, cruthú and khoros. GAPS IT ANSWERS, of the fifteen the research found (resonance-forosnai/docs/THE-EFFECTS-RESEARCH.md §5, as the plan reads them): 9 and 14, logic node-only or weak scripting and no interactive or data-driven output — logic is a modulation, a signal mapped to a key by a law as data, and an effect may declare a map onto the effects engine''s own tokens, so an effect can drive an interface as readily as a picture. WALL NAMED ON THE SAME PAGE: face signals are theophany''s reading; this studio maps them and never reads a camera itself. MARK: small, step 2 of "The order and the marks", beside the-wear; steps 1 to 6 need no app. One hand and one verifier, proofs in the water''s own folder, mirrored into its consumers by copy with a MIRROR.md. Described 2026-09-15 in resonance-forosnai/docs/THE-FOROSNAI-PLAN.md, the table under "What still needs imagining", drawn at KP''s ⚛ word: "then outline what flowing or imagined stand alone waters already exist to serve and what ones still need imagined." NAMED BY KP 2026-09-15, the line verbatim: "3- the-dynamics". Seeded imagined 2026-09-15 at KP''s ⚛ word.',
 'a platform hand, at KP''s ⚛ word',
 'Awen', '🎢'),

-- 4 · the-transition
('The Transition', 'the-transition', 'combine',
 'The transition, between two sources over a span. Its kinds are laws as data: the cut, the dissolve, and the wipe as a mask moving under a curve. In go two sources, a kind, a span and a moment. Out comes the blend of the two at that moment, or the plan for that blend. The blend is resolved at a millisecond, and the span''s edges are half-open. Nothing is drawn here; the blend, or the plan for it, is what the consumer is handed.',
 'resonance-awen/tools/the-transition', 'imagined',
 (select id from public.atoms where atom_word = 'transition'), null, null,
 'WHAT STANDS BESIDE IT, as the plan marks it: the-kampyle (flowing); the-scene''s switch with its timing (imagined). CONSUMERS: forosnaí first — Part Two''s bench holds the waters as nodes, and Part Two''s timeline runs the-kampyle between keys under the graph. Then the sibling studios the charter names as wearing what is made here: sceal for the moving picture, ardan for the stage, khoros for what streams, sistrum for sound, theophany for the face, cruthú for the still picture. MARK: small, step 5 of "The order and the marks", beside the-glyphs; steps 1 to 6 need no app. One hand and one verifier, proofs in the water''s own folder, mirrored into its consumers by copy with a MIRROR.md; a water whose consumer is itself imagined is mirrored the day that consumer is built, and the-scene is imagined. Described 2026-09-15 in resonance-forosnai/docs/THE-FOROSNAI-PLAN.md, the table under "What still needs imagining", drawn at KP''s ⚛ word: "then outline what flowing or imagined stand alone waters already exist to serve and what ones still need imagined." NAMED BY KP 2026-09-15, the line verbatim: "4- the-transition". Seeded imagined 2026-09-15 at KP''s ⚛ word.',
 'a platform hand, at KP''s ⚛ word',
 'Awen', '🔦'),

-- 5 · the-screen
('The Screen', 'the-screen', 'transform',
 'The filter. Arithmetic on a plane of pixels, described as data: a convolution kernel, which is the blur, the sharpen and the edge; a colour matrix; a per-pixel law; and a displacement by a map. In go a plane and a filter''s description. Out comes a new plane. The filter is applied to the plane and returns a new plane, never the input, so the plane handed in stands as it was. These are the pure picture effects: the four descriptions carry the arithmetic.',
 'resonance-awen/tools/the-screen', 'imagined',
 (select id from public.atoms where atom_word = 'screen'), null, null,
 'WHAT STANDS BESIDE IT, as the plan marks it: the blur is already the-mask''s (imagined), and looks are the-grade''s (imagined); the kernel, the colour matrix and the displacement are new, and the colour half is a harvest of cruthú''s adjust.ts levels, curves, hue and saturation, which stand. CONSUMERS: forosnaí first — Part Two''s preview runs the filter''s description compiled to a shader where the host has one and as arithmetic where it does not, the canvas holding the planes; sceal, whose first effect in Part Three is a background, the-mask and the-screen, the blur behind the person; cruthú, whose adjust.ts arithmetic the colour half harvests. Then the rest of the siblings the charter names: sistrum, ardan, theophany and khoros. WHAT IS SHARED: the plan''s "What is shared, and so has its home in the spring" leaves the shader compiled from the-screen''s description to this water itself — text in and text out, and so the-screen''s own to emit — while the draw of a plan onto a canvas or WebGL is another water, born in the spring the day a second studio needs it, with forosnaí wearing the mirror. WALL NAMED ON THE SAME PAGE: a filter described as data runs as arithmetic anywhere and as a shader only where the host compiles one; the shader is the dress, and the plan''s cost is what keeps the arithmetic road honest. MARK: medium, step 4 of "The order and the marks" — harvested where cruthú and the-mask already hold the arithmetic; steps 1 to 6 need no app. One hand and one verifier, proofs in the water''s own folder, mirrored into its consumers by copy with a MIRROR.md. Described 2026-09-15 in resonance-forosnai/docs/THE-FOROSNAI-PLAN.md, the table under "What still needs imagining", drawn at KP''s ⚛ word: "then outline what flowing or imagined stand alone waters already exist to serve and what ones still need imagined." NAMED BY KP 2026-09-15, the line verbatim: "5- the-screen". Seeded imagined 2026-09-15 at KP''s ⚛ word.',
 'a platform hand, at KP''s ⚛ word',
 'Awen', '🪟'),

-- 6 · the-particles
('The Particles', 'the-particles', 'arrange',
 'The particles. An emitter held as laws, as data: the rate at which particles are born, the lifetime each one carries, the ranges of its birth position and its velocity, the forces that act on it, and the look it wears per age. In go an emitter''s laws, a seed and a moment. Out come the particles at that moment, as keys. The field is resolved to positions and looks at a millisecond from a seed the consumer hands in, since randomness is not a water''s to make; the same seed gives the same field.',
 'resonance-awen/tools/the-particles', 'imagined',
 (select id from public.atoms where atom_word = 'particle'), null, null,
 'THE NAME IS PLURAL AND THE ATOM IS THE ROOT: `particle` already carries "s" in its modifiers, so the plural is the modifiers'' work (the-scrolls precedent, 055). WHAT STANDS BESIDE IT, as the plan marks it: nothing; the-hlutr for the drawing of lots (flowing); and it is two-dimensional in the plane, so it is no second geometry beside the-stereos. CONSUMERS: forosnaí first — Part Two''s bench holds the waters as nodes with their parameters read from each node''s tree, and Part Two''s preview draws the planes on the canvas, the cost deciding the preview''s size before the frame is drawn. Then the sibling studios the charter names as wearing what is made here: sceal for the moving picture, ardan for the stage, cruthú for the still picture, theophany for the face, khoros for what streams, sistrum for sound. MARK: medium, step 6 of "The order and the marks", the last of the six steps that need no app. One hand and one verifier, proofs in the water''s own folder, mirrored into its consumers by copy with a MIRROR.md. Described 2026-09-15 in resonance-forosnai/docs/THE-FOROSNAI-PLAN.md, the table under "What still needs imagining", drawn at KP''s ⚛ word: "then outline what flowing or imagined stand alone waters already exist to serve and what ones still need imagined." NAMED BY KP 2026-09-15, the line verbatim, the spelling KP''s own: "6- the-paritles"; the name is the-particles. Seeded imagined 2026-09-15 at KP''s ⚛ word.',
 'a platform hand, at KP''s ⚛ word',
 'Awen', '🫧'),

-- 7 · the-glyphs
('The Glyphs', 'the-glyphs', 'arrange',
 'The letters in motion. Text stands as parts — glyphs, words and lines — and each part carries a track of keys. The parts are laid by arithmetic. The reveal, the fall and the drift are laws upon those tracks: each names what the parts do across time, part by part. What a face needs to read stays readable. In go text, a layout, tracks of keys and a moment. Out comes each part''s transform at that moment, one transform for every part the text was broken into.',
 'resonance-awen/tools/the-glyphs', 'imagined',
 (select id from public.atoms where atom_word = 'glyph'), null, null,
 'THE NAME IS PLURAL AND THE ATOM IS THE ROOT: `glyph` already carries "s" in its modifiers, so the plural is the modifiers'' work (the-scrolls precedent, 055). WHAT STANDS BESIDE IT, as the plan marks it: nothing lays glyphs; the-overlay''s layout and wrapping (imagined). WHAT FLOWS BESIDE IT in Part One''s table: the-effects-engine''s four laws — A0, a static twin for every motion, calm never urgent, per-reader intensity — and the-two-eyes'' per-reader toggles, effects intensity among them. CONSUMERS: forosnaí first — Part Two''s timeline carries the tracks of keys each part rides, with the-kampyle between keys and groups as nodes; sceal, where the-overlay puts titles and captions on a cut''s clock, and ardan. Then the rest of the siblings the charter names: sistrum, theophany, cruthú and khoros. MARK: medium, step 5 of "The order and the marks", beside the-transition; steps 1 to 6 need no app. One hand and one verifier, proofs in the water''s own folder, mirrored into its consumers by copy with a MIRROR.md; a water whose consumer is itself imagined is mirrored the day that consumer is built, and the-overlay is imagined. Described 2026-09-15 in resonance-forosnai/docs/THE-FOROSNAI-PLAN.md, the table under "What still needs imagining", drawn at KP''s ⚛ word: "then outline what flowing or imagined stand alone waters already exist to serve and what ones still need imagined." NAMED BY KP 2026-09-15, the line verbatim: "7- the-glyphs". Seeded imagined 2026-09-15 at KP''s ⚛ word.',
 'a platform hand, at KP''s ⚛ word',
 'Awen', '🪪'),

-- 8 · the-resonance
('The Resonance', 'the-resonance', 'capture',
 'The tracker. A point or a region is followed across frames by template matching on planes within a search window: the region names what is followed and the window names where it is sought, so the search is bounded by the caller''s own declaration. The match carries its confidence, and where there is not one peak the water refuses rather than guesses. The track is kept as keys, so a thing can ride what it follows. In go two planes, a region and a window. Out come the offset and its confidence, or a refusal; and the track.',
 'resonance-awen/tools/the-resonance', 'imagined',
 (select id from public.atoms where atom_word = 'resonance'), null, null,
 'WHAT STANDS BESIDE IT, as the plan marks it: the-alignment''s cross-correlation on samples is the shape, one dimension up (imagined); nothing on planes. CONSUMERS: forosnaí first — the track is keys, so a thing can ride what it follows through any node on Part Two''s bench. Then the sibling studios the charter names as wearing what is made here: sceal for the moving picture, ardan for the stage, theophany for the face, khoros for what streams, cruthú for the still picture, sistrum for sound. MARK: large, step 9 of "The order and the marks", after the app''s own steps. WALL NAMED ON THE SAME PAGE: the tracker is the one large water and comes last; nothing in Part Two waits on it. One hand and one verifier, proofs in the water''s own folder, mirrored into its consumers by copy with a MIRROR.md; a water whose consumer is itself imagined is mirrored the day that consumer is built. Described 2026-09-15 in resonance-forosnai/docs/THE-FOROSNAI-PLAN.md, the table under "What still needs imagining", drawn at KP''s ⚛ word: "then outline what flowing or imagined stand alone waters already exist to serve and what ones still need imagined." NAMED BY KP 2026-09-15, the line verbatim: "8- the-resonance". Seeded imagined 2026-09-15 at KP''s ⚛ word.',
 'a platform hand, at KP''s ⚛ word',
 'Awen', '👀'),

-- 9 · the-wear
('The Wear', 'the-wear', 'witness',
 'The wear. What a host must provide for an effect to be worn: the signals, the planes, the sounds, the rates and the size. The requirement is read from the effect''s document and checked against what a host declares. In go an effect and a host''s declaration. Out comes worn, or the named lack. The answer is whole, and the refusal is named before anything runs rather than after it has run. The requirement is data, and a rejection is never a surprise.',
 'resonance-awen/tools/the-wear', 'imagined',
 (select id from public.atoms where atom_word = 'wear'), null, null,
 'WHAT STANDS BESIDE IT, as the plan marks it: the shape of the-lok''s answer, open or shut with the reason named, and of the-kinema''s refusal by name and the-delivery''s (flowing, flowing, imagined). CONSUMERS: forosnaí first — Part Two''s sources room, where each source declares what it gives in the-wear''s terms: a still from cruthú, a clip or a take from sceal, a lane from sistrum, the camera through theophany''s reading, the microphone through the-awenydd, a beat from the-metronome; and Part Two''s wear room, where the host declarations of each sibling studio are read from disk and the-wear''s answer is shown per sibling before the maker carries it. Then every sibling studio the charter names as wearing what is made here: sistrum, sceal, ardan, theophany, cruthú and khoros, each of which declares its host. GAPS IT ANSWERS, of the fifteen the research found (resonance-forosnai/docs/THE-EFFECTS-RESEARCH.md §5, as the plan reads them): 4, 5, 7 and 8, one row in the plan (slow previews, crashes, hardware the maker does not have, caps discovered by rejection), of which this water answers the caps: the caps are the effect''s own declared requirements, checked before wear, never a surprise. MARK: small, step 2 of "The order and the marks", beside the-dynamics; steps 1 to 6 need no app. One hand and one verifier, proofs in the water''s own folder, mirrored into its consumers by copy with a MIRROR.md. Described 2026-09-15 in resonance-forosnai/docs/THE-FOROSNAI-PLAN.md, the table under "What still needs imagining", drawn at KP''s ⚛ word: "then outline what flowing or imagined stand alone waters already exist to serve and what ones still need imagined." NAMED BY KP 2026-09-15, the line verbatim: "9- the-wear". Seeded imagined 2026-09-15 at KP''s ⚛ word.',
